  "configuration_id": "config_014",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_021 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) is the current best at 0.629 acc. In singleprofile, concat (0.535) and weighted (0.532) fusion were nearly equivalent, but we have no multiprofile data on weighted fusion. Question: Does weighted fusion interact differently with multiprofile avgpool aggregation than concat does? This is a single-variable change from the current best, isolating the fusion mechanism. Rationale: Under a limited budget, testing one design axis at a time from the best-known configuration is the most efficient way to determine whether a simple swap can improve performance or confirm that concat is already optimal in this regime. If weighted fusion matches or exceeds concat, it opens a new axis (e.g., combining with alternative RNA encoders); if it underperforms, we can rule out weighted fusion and focus remaining budget on other untested dimensions (e.g., image encoder or RNA encoder in multiprofile)."
}

